# Copy to .env (gitignored — never commit real credentials) in this same directory. Read fresh
# per call by EnvConfig, keyed to this tool's own name ('railway-safe-cli') — not shared with any
# other tool's .env.

# One token env var per registered auth profile (see auth-profiles.json's "envVar" field). Use a
# Railway PROJECT token (project settings -> Tokens -> New Token, scoped to one
# project+environment), never an account-wide API token — a profile's blast radius should never
# exceed the one project/environment it names. Injected into the railway CLI's child process
# environment as RAILWAY_TOKEN, never passed as a CLI argument.
RAILWAY_SAFE_CLI_EXAMPLE_PROJECT_TOKEN=""

# Optional: absolute path to the railway binary, when it isn't on this MCP server process's PATH.
# Defaults to "railway" resolved via PATH when unset/empty.
RAILWAY_CLI_PATH=""

# Optional: per-call timeout in milliseconds for the spawned railway process. Defaults to 60000
# when unset/empty or not a valid number.
RAILWAY_CLI_TIMEOUT_MS=""
